'''''Luzula forsteri''''', commonly known as '''southern wood-rush''',<ref name=BSBI07>{{BSBI 2007 |accessdate=2014-10-17 }}</ref> is a species of [[perennial plant]] in [[Juncaceae]] family that is native to [[Europe]], [[north Africa]] and [[western Asia]]. There is a record of it having been collected at Salem, Oregon in 1910.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://plants.usda.gov/java/profile?symbol=LUFO6|title=''Luzula forsteri'' (Sm.) DC.|publisher=PLANTS Profile|work=[[United States Department of Agriculture|USDA]]|access-date=April 5, 2013}}</ref>

The species was named for [[Edward Forster the Younger]] (1765–1849).<ref>James Edward Smith. Flora Britannica. 1804. vol. 3: p. 1359</ref>

